      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360AD Control of a company",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-360ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n(b) the definition of associate in section 360AB of this Act\napplies instead.\n360AE  When a person is in a position to exercise control of a facility\n(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (the first person) is in a\nposition to exercise control of a facility if:\n(a) the first person legally or beneficially owns the facility\n(whether alone or together with one or more other persons);\nor\n(b) the first person is in a position, either alone or together with\nan associate of the first person and whether directly or\nindirectly:\n(i) to exercise control of the operation of all or part of the\nfacility; or\n(ii) to exercise control of the selection of the kinds of\nservices that are supplied using the facility; or\n(iii) to exercise control of the supply of services using the\nfacility; or\n(c) a company other than the first person legally or beneficially\nowns the facility (whether alone or together with one or more\nother persons), and:\n(i) the first person is in a position, either alone or together\nwith an associate of the first person, to exercise control\nof the company; or\n(ii) the first person, either alone or together with an\nassociate of the first person, is in a position to veto any\naction taken by the board of directors of the company;\nor\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n(b) the definition of associate in section 360AB of this Act\napplies instead.\n360AE  When a person is in a position to exercise control of a facility\n(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (the first person) is in a\nposition to exercise control of a facility if:\n(a) the first person legally or beneficially owns the facility\n(whether alone or together with one or more other persons);\nor\n(b) the first person is in a position, either alone or together with\nan associate of the first person and whether directly or\nindirectly:\n(i) to exercise control of the operation of all or part of the\nfacility; or\n(ii) to exercise control of the selection of the kinds of\nservices that are supplied using the facility; or\n(iii) to exercise control of the supply of services using the\nfacility; or\n(c) a company other than the first person legally or beneficially\nowns the facility (whether alone or together with one or more\nother persons), and:\n(i) the first person is in a position, either alone or together\nwith an associate of the first person, to exercise control\nof the company; or\n(ii) the first person, either alone or together with an\nassociate of the first person, is in a position to veto any\naction taken by the board of directors of the company;\nor\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ad-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ad-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ad-ss-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffe55e3eb155ab5a271643ce7ad1e217ddd1b335c84aeb39f0d821278fa4091d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-360ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360AD Control of a company",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n(b) the definition of associate in section 360AB of this Act\napplies instead.\n360AE  When a person is in a position to exercise control of a facility\n(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (the first person) is in a\nposition to exercise control of a facility if:\n(a) the first person legally or beneficially owns the facility\n(whether alone or together with one or more other persons);\nor\n(b) the first person is in a position, either alone or together with\nan associate of the first person and whether directly or\nindirectly:\n(i) to exercise control of the operation of all or part of the\nfacility; or\n(ii) to exercise control of the selection of the kinds of\nservices that are supplied using the facility; or\n(iii) to exercise control of the supply of services using the\nfacility; or\n(c) a company other than the first person legally or beneficially\nowns the facility (whether alone or together with one or more\nother persons), and:\n(i) the first person is in a position, either alone or together\nwith an associate of the first person, to exercise control\nof the company; or\n(ii) the first person, either alone or together with an\nassociate of the first person, is in a position to veto any\naction taken by the board of directors of the company;\nor\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers"
    },
