        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c797554ba1ee2f34c795e3b138885b84903c61243e0d7c8c89dddce8f583710",
      "skos:note": "Determines the question of control of a company under Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992. A person is in a position to exercise control of a facility if they meet certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-360ad-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360AD(1) Control of a company",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (the first person) is in a\nposition to exercise control of a facility if:\n(a) the first person legally or beneficially owns the facility\n(whether alone or together with one or more other persons);\nor\n(b) the first person is in a position, either alone or together with\nan associate of the first person and whether directly or\nindirectly:\n(i) to exercise control of the operation of all or part of the\nfacility; or\n(ii) to exercise control of the selection of the kinds of\nservices that are supplied using the facility; or\n(iii) to exercise control of the supply of services using the\nfacility; or\n(c) a company other than the first person legally or beneficially\nowns the facility (whether alone or together with one or more\nother persons), and:\n(i) the first person is in a position, either alone or together\nwith an associate of the first person, to exercise control\nof the company; or\n(ii) the first person, either alone or together with an\nassociate of the first person, is in a position to veto any\naction taken by the board of directors of the company;\nor\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers"
    },
