    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Subsections 360H(14), (15), (16) and (17)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(14) A carrier may, by writing, vary a declaration made by the carrier\nunder this section, so long as the ACMA has approved the\nvariation under subsection (15).\n(15) The ACMA may, on application made by a carrier, approve the\nvariation of a declaration made by the carrier under this section.\n(16) An application under subsection (15) must:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA; and\n(c) be accompanied by such information (if any) as is specified\nunder subsection (17); and\n(d) be accompanied by such documents (if any) as are specified\nunder subsection (17).\n(17) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument:\n(a) specify the information that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15); or\n(b) specify the documents that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(17A) If, under subsection (14), a carrier varies a declaration made by the\ncarrier under this section, the carrier must:\n(a) give a copy of the variation to the ACMA; and\n(b) do so within 10 business days after making the variation.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(14) A carrier may, by writing, vary a declaration made by the carrier\nunder this section, so long as the ACMA has approved the\nvariation under subsection (15).\n(15) The ACMA may, on application made by a carrier, approve the\nvariation of a declaration made by the carrier under this section.\n(16) An application under subsection (15) must:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA; and\n(c) be accompanied by such information (if any) as is specified\nunder subsection (17); and\n(d) be accompanied by such documents (if any) as are specified\nunder subsection (17).\n(17) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument:\n(a) specify the information that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15); or\n(b) specify the documents that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(17A) If, under subsection (14), a carrier varies a declaration made by the\ncarrier under this section, the carrier must:\n(a) give a copy of the variation to the ACMA; and\n(b) do so within 10 business days after making the variation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53-ss-14"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53-ss-15"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53-ss-16"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53-ss-17"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-53-ss-17a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Subsections 360H(14), (15), (16) and (17)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n(14) A carrier may, by writing, vary a declaration made by the carrier\nunder this section, so long as the ACMA has approved the\nvariation under subsection (15).\n(15) The ACMA may, on application made by a carrier, approve the\nvariation of a declaration made by the carrier under this section.\n(16) An application under subsection (15) must:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA; and\n(c) be accompanied by such information (if any) as is specified\nunder subsection (17); and\n(d) be accompanied by such documents (if any) as are specified\nunder subsection (17).\n(17) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument:\n(a) specify the information that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15); or\n(b) specify the documents that must accompany an application\nunder subsection (15).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(17A) If, under subsection (14), a carrier varies a declaration made by the\ncarrier under this section, the carrier must:\n(a) give a copy of the variation to the ACMA; and\n(b) do so within 10 business days after making the variation."
    },
