      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n(a) a specified development area mentioned in subsection (1) is\nnot a nominated service area for the purposes of this Part;\nand\n(b) a specified area is a nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n(a) a specified development area mentioned in subsection (1) is\nnot a nominated service area for the purposes of this Part;\nand\n(b) a specified area is a nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-76"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-76-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da5e0d3fbc91571f71473f2428e8ae6255a1e75b852dbea8c73879f8cb03b73e",
      "skos:note": "Minister may declare development areas not nominated service areas or vice versa."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-76-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76(4) At the end of section 360J",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n(a) a specified development area mentioned in subsection (1) is\nnot a nominated service area for the purposes of this Part;\nand\n(b) a specified area is a nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part.\nNote 1:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-76-ss-4-norm",
