    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Subsections 360Q(2) and (2A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(2B) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(2B) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-110-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-110-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-110-ss-2b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "539efa85cf0c2d5371e1fca5b7c2fae9542891ca7c1d338008eace1bd8888db4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Subsections 360Q(2) and (2A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n(2B) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
