    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-119",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "119 At the end of section 360Q",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-119"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nResponse to request\n(11) If a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1):\n(a) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) notify the carriage service provider that the statutory\ninfrastructure provider will fulfil the request; or\n(ii) refuse the request; and\n(b) do so within:\n(i) 10 business days after receiving the request; or\n(ii) if a longer period is specified under subsection (12)—\nthat longer period.\n(12) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a period for\nthe purposes of subparagraph (11)(b)(ii).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNotification of refusal of request\n(13) If:\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1); and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(b) the fulfilment of the request would affect an end-user at\nparticular premises; and\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider refuses the request;\nthen:\n(d) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) give written notice of the refusal, and the reasons for the\nrefusal, to the carriage service provider; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after the refusal; and\n(e) if the carriage service provider receives the notice—the\ncarriage service provider must:\n(i) give a copy of the notice to the end-user; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nResponse to request\n(11) If a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1):\n(a) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) notify the carriage service provider that the statutory\ninfrastructure provider will fulfil the request; or\n(ii) refuse the request; and\n(b) do so within:\n(i) 10 business days after receiving the request; or\n(ii) if a longer period is specified under subsection (12)—\nthat longer period.\n(12) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a period for\nthe purposes of subparagraph (11)(b)(ii).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNotification of refusal of request\n(13) If:\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1); and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(b) the fulfilment of the request would affect an end-user at\nparticular premises; and\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider refuses the request;\nthen:\n(d) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) give written notice of the refusal, and the reasons for the\nrefusal, to the carriage service provider; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after the refusal; and\n(e) if the carriage service provider receives the notice—the\ncarriage service provider must:\n(i) give a copy of the notice to the end-user; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-119-ss-11"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-119-ss-12"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-119-ss-13"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30889dfcae76f68f282943bb718e55ae5f47316b66e68aec9588df48220bf6b6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-119",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "119 At the end of section 360Q",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nResponse to request\n(11) If a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1):\n(a) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) notify the carriage service provider that the statutory\ninfrastructure provider will fulfil the request; or\n(ii) refuse the request; and\n(b) do so within:\n(i) 10 business days after receiving the request; or\n(ii) if a longer period is specified under subsection (12)—\nthat longer period.\n(12) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a period for\nthe purposes of subparagraph (11)(b)(ii).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNotification of refusal of request\n(13) If:\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1); and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\nNo. 36, 2024\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\n(b) the fulfilment of the request would affect an end-user at\nparticular premises; and\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider refuses the request;\nthen:\n(d) the statutory infrastructure provider must:\n(i) give written notice of the refusal, and the reasons for the\nrefusal, to the carriage service provider; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after the refusal; and\n(e) if the carriage service provider receives the notice—the\ncarriage service provider must:\n(i) give a copy of the notice to the end-user; and\n(ii) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-119-ss-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "119(11) At the end of section 360Q",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-119-ss-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
