    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360RA Rules may impose additional notification obligations on a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-360ra"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "statutory infrastructure provider\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n(a) apply to a statutory infrastructure provider that is subject to\nan obligation under subsection 360R(2) or (3); and\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\nstatutory infrastructure provider.\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) Rules under subsection (1) may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the rules.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nCompliance\n(6) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers",
      "skos:definition": "statutory infrastructure provider\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n(a) apply to a statutory infrastructure provider that is subject to\nan obligation under subsection 360R(2) or (3); and\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\nstatutory infrastructure provider.\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) Rules under subsection (1) may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the rules.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nCompliance\n(6) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-1-sec-360ra-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "acf0135577a20a25c4f30dff08cb955e86a28ca24f75a31f2abbf82ffc142867"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-1-sec-360ra",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360RA Rules may impose additional notification obligations on a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "statutory infrastructure provider\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n(a) apply to a statutory infrastructure provider that is subject to\nan obligation under subsection 360R(2) or (3); and\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\nstatutory infrastructure provider.\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) Rules under subsection (1) may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the rules.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nCompliance\n(6) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\nSchedule 1  Statutory infrastructure providers"
    },
