      },
      "cml:conclusionText": "A remedial notice must be known as a remedial notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JB Contents of remedial notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A remedial notice given to a person by the ACMA must state:\n(a) that the ACMA reasonably believes that the person:\n(i) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n(ii) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention\nwill continue or be repeated; or\n(iii) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty\nprovision; and\n(b) the provision the ACMA believes is being, has been, or is\nlikely to be, contravened; and\n(c) briefly, how the provision is being, has been, or is likely to\nbe, contravened; and\n(d) the period within which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n(2) The remedial notice may include directions concerning the\nmeasures to be taken to:\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n(3) The period stated for compliance with the remedial notice must be\nreasonable in all the circumstances.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A remedial notice given to a person by the ACMA must state:\n(a) that the ACMA reasonably believes that the person:\n(i) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n(ii) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention\nwill continue or be repeated; or\n(iii) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty\nprovision; and\n(b) the provision the ACMA believes is being, has been, or is\nlikely to be, contravened; and\n(c) briefly, how the provision is being, has been, or is likely to\nbe, contravened; and\n(d) the period within which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n(2) The remedial notice may include directions concerning the\nmeasures to be taken to:\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n(3) The period stated for compliance with the remedial notice must be\nreasonable in all the circumstances.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d68ab43ad3bd5b745a537c1d547f6b8587d33c2cc75316b2b22dfc44c8aeaad"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372JB Contents of remedial notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A remedial notice given to a person by the ACMA must state:\n(a) that the ACMA reasonably believes that the person:\n(i) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n(ii) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention\nwill continue or be repeated; or\n(iii) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty\nprovision; and\n(b) the provision the ACMA believes is being, has been, or is\nlikely to be, contravened; and\n(c) briefly, how the provision is being, has been, or is likely to\nbe, contravened; and\n(d) the period within which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n(2) The remedial notice may include directions concerning the\nmeasures to be taken to:\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n(3) The period stated for compliance with the remedial notice must be\nreasonable in all the circumstances."
    },
