    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JF Revocation of remedial notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and\n(b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the\nACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer\nrequired for the purposes of requiring the person to:\n(i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty\nprovision; or\n(ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil\npenalty provision from occurring; or\n(iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention,\nor likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty\nprovision;\nthe ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nnotice.\n(2) In this section, compliance period means the period stated in the\nremedial notice under section 372JB, and includes that period as\nextended under section 372JD.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and\n(b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the\nACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer\nrequired for the purposes of requiring the person to:\n(i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty\nprovision; or\n(ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil\npenalty provision from occurring; or\n(iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention,\nor likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty\nprovision;\nthe ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nnotice.\n(2) In this section, compliance period means the period stated in the\nremedial notice under section 372JB, and includes that period as\nextended under section 372JD.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jf-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "00b7dfb884dcd1dd4189f68e83248bde57c05d8115ba6fce4620a18d0fb90d6b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jf",
