      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and\n(b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the\nACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer\nrequired for the purposes of requiring the person to:\n(i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty\nprovision; or\n(ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil\npenalty provision from occurring; or\n(iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention,\nor likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty\nprovision;\nthe ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nnotice."
    },
