    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JG Formal irregularities or defects in remedial notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "A remedial notice is not invalid only because of:\n(a) a formal defect or irregularity in the notice unless the defect\nor irregularity causes or is likely to cause substantial\ninjustice; or\n(b) a failure to use the correct name of the person to whom the\nnotice is issued if the notice sufficiently identifies the person.",
      "skos:definition": "A remedial notice is not invalid only because of:\n(a) a formal defect or irregularity in the notice unless the defect\nor irregularity causes or is likely to cause substantial\ninjustice; or\n(b) a failure to use the correct name of the person to whom the\nnotice is issued if the notice sufficiently identifies the person.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b2993880cb3b8ab6f1e8ad48653585c403fea3ea4e865b288765fa1b83dbddc",
      "skos:note": "A remedial notice is not invalid due to formal defects or irregularities unless they cause substantial injustice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372JG Formal irregularities or defects in remedial notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "A remedial notice is not invalid only because of:\n(a) a formal defect or irregularity in the notice unless the defect\nor irregularity causes or is likely to cause substantial\ninjustice; or\n(b) a failure to use the correct name of the person to whom the\nnotice is issued if the notice sufficiently identifies the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to issue a valid notice",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The notice must be issued in accordance with the law.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The notice is invalid if it does not meet the requirements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to issue a notice despite formal defects or irregularities",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The law allows for the issuance of notices despite formal defects or irregularities.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A remedial notice is not invalid due to formal defects or irregularities unless they cause substantial injustice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to issue a valid notice despite failure to use the correct name",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The law requires the issuance of notices in accordance with the law.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A remedial notice is not invalid due to a failure to use the correct name if it sufficiently identifies the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jg-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The notice must be issued within a specific time frame",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The law requires the issuance of notices in accordance with the law.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A remedial notice is not invalid due to formal defects or irregularities unless they cause substantial injustice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JH Designated civil penalty provision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\nSchedule 2  Deployment of optical fibre\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNo. 36, 2024\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n(h) subsection 372G(5).",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\nSchedule 2  Deployment of optical fibre\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNo. 36, 2024\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n(h) subsection 372G(5).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jh-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1959c7df1ed38977beef9512059265364fcca23700e3125df1453cc33b052d8c",
      "skos:note": "List of designated civil penalty provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-2-sec-372jh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372JH Designated civil penalty provision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\nSchedule 2  Deployment of optical fibre\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Enhancing Consumer\nSafeguards and Other Measures) Act 2024\nNo. 36, 2024\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n(h) subsection 372G(5)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-2-sec-372jh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
