    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-3-sec-59da-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59DA(4) Disclosure of information that relates to the affairs of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-3-sec-59da-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(b)(x), (2)(b)(x)\nand (3)(b)(x).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(b)(x), (2)(b)(x)\nand (3)(b)(x).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-3-sec-59da"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-3-sec-59da-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87ae7e6ec422dd5c6a673e1620ace4136a8f0e79d33fa2a79c4684315bf0d474",
      "skos:note": "Determine matters for disclosure purposes",
      "dc:references": [
        "subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-3-sec-59da-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59DA(4) Disclosure of information that relates to the affairs of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(b)(x), (2)(b)(x)\nand (3)(b)(x).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901."
    },
