    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572M Guidelines relating to infringement notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-5-sec-572m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2024a00036.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2024a00036.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "ACMA guidelines\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(3) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (1) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (2).\nACCC guidelines\n(4) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chairperson of\nthe ACCC, or a member of the staff of the ACCC appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (5).\n(5) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines for\nthe purposes of subsection (4).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(6) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (4) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (5).",
      "skos:definition": "ACMA guidelines\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(3) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (1) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (2).\nACCC guidelines\n(4) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chairperson of\nthe ACCC, or a member of the staff of the ACCC appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (5).\n(5) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines for\nthe purposes of subsection (4).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(6) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (4) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (5).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f2955b8a523c4cb9310453e19e64d9074568a7c8f5ecc0297c7de06b8b84a45"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2024a00036#sch-5-sec-572m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572M Guidelines relating to infringement notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "ACMA guidelines\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(3) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (1) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (2).\nACCC guidelines\n(4) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chairperson of\nthe ACCC, or a member of the staff of the ACCC appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (5).\n(5) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines for\nthe purposes of subsection (4).\nNote:\nFor consultation requirements, see section 17 (consultation) of the\nLegislation Act 2003.\n(6) An authorised infringement notice officer mentioned in\nsubsection (4) must not give an infringement notice to a person\nunless guidelines are in force under subsection (5)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2024a00036-sch-5-sec-572m-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
